---
title: 'Standard Library'
description: 'The Zena standard library — every module, extracted from its source.'
permalink: '/reference/stdlib/'
---

<p class="api-import">
  {{ "import {HashMap} from 'zena:collections';" | highlight('zena') | safe }}
</p>

<p>
  Every module below ships with the compiler and is importable by name, with
  no dependency to declare. These pages are extracted from the standard
  library's own source, so a signature here is the signature the compiler
  checks against.
</p>

<h2 id="modules">Modules</h2>

<div class="api-module-list">
  {% for module in api.stdlib %}
    <div class="api-module-entry">
      <a href="{{ module.url }}"><code>{{ module.id }}</code></a>
      {% if module.doc.summary %}
        <span class="api-module-summary">{{ module.doc.summary }}</span>
      {% elif module.count %}
        <span class="api-module-summary"
          >{{ module.count }} declaration{% if module.count != 1 %}s{% endif %}</span
        >
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
